## Core Architectural Pillars

All mobile applications delivered across the enterprise must implement the four foundational architectural pillars:

| Architectural Pillar | Standard Enforced | Engineering Purpose | Verification Method |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Clean Architecture** | Strict 4-layer model (Presentation, Domain, Data, Core). Domain layer has zero external dependencies. | Decouples pure business rules from volatile UI frameworks and databases. Guarantees 100% portable domain testing. | Danger PR code structure audit & unit tests. |
| **Network Resilience** | Threshold-based Circuit Breaker wrapping all remote HTTP calls with local offline cache fallback. | Prevents cascading connection timeouts, stops battery drain, and maintains offline usability in dead zones. | Automated unit tests with simulated 500/timeout responses. |
| **Remote Config & Flags** | Dynamic feature flags and emergency kill switches decoupled from store release cycles. | Enables staged percentage rollouts (5% &rarr; 25% &rarr; 100%) and instant kill-switching without waiting for store review. | Integration with enterprise feature flag client. |
| **Hardware-Backed Security** | OAuth2/OIDC SSO tokens stored in hardware KeyStore (Android) or Keychain (iOS). Zero plain-text credentials. | Protects against binary reverse engineering, memory dumping, and stolen device credential exfiltration. | Automated SAST/DAST security scanning. |

