<Aside type="tip" title="ARCHITECTURE MANDATE">
The 4-layer clean architecture pattern is mandatory across all enterprise iOS, Android, and React Native applications. By strictly decoupling Presentation, Domain, Data, and Core Infrastructure into distinct layers governed by Dependency Inversion, applications achieve 100% portable business logic, predictable unidirectional data flow, and isolated unit testability.
</Aside>

## Four-Layer Clean Architecture Model

Every enterprise mobile codebase must strictly adhere to the four architectural layers defined below:

| Architectural Layer | Primary Responsibilities | Allowed Inward Dependencies | Prohibited Elements |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Presentation Layer** | Renders reactive declarative UI views, captures user input, and manages screen lifecycle state. | Depends only on the **Domain Layer** (executes Use Cases and observes state). | Direct SQL queries, raw HTTP client calls, network DTO models. |
| **Domain Layer** | Encapsulates pure enterprise business rules, entity models, and abstract repository contracts. | **Zero external dependencies.** Pure language code (zero Android, iOS, or React imports). | UI widgets, database drivers, third-party platform SDKs. |
| **Data Layer** | Implements domain repository contracts. Coordinates remote APIs with offline local databases. | Depends on the **Domain Layer** (implements interfaces) and **Core Infrastructure**. | Direct UI rendering logic, lifecycle observation, business rule mutation. |
| **Core Infrastructure** | Shared cross-cutting foundations: SSO Auth, Resilience Circuit Breaker, Datadog Telemetry, KeyStore. | Standalone shared modules consumed by Data and Presentation layers. | Feature-specific business domain logic. Must remain universally reusable. |

---

