<Aside type="tip" title="RELEASE GOVERNANCE MANDATE">
All new features and user-facing capabilities must be shipped behind dynamic runtime feature flags evaluated via the Unleash Mobile Edge Proxy. Code is deployed continuously in dark mode and released progressively without waiting for app store binary review queues.
</Aside>

## Mobile Release Decoupling

Coupling feature releases directly to compiled binary updates introduces operational challenges:
* **Store Review Latency:** Emergency bug fixes can take 24 to 72 hours for store approval across Apple App Store and Google Play.
* **Variable Client Adoption:** Users update apps asynchronously, leaving a fraction of users on legacy binaries.
* **All-or-Nothing Blast Radius:** Releasing directly to 100% of devices risks service degradation if backend services experience unexpected load spikes.

The enterprise mandates **Unleash Proxy Client** to decouple binary deployment from feature activation. Code is delivered dark in sprint builds and activated dynamically at runtime.

---

## Unleash Mobile Edge Proxy Topology

Mobile clients must never connect directly to the core Unleash database or management console. All mobile applications communicate exclusively with the **Unleash Edge Proxy**:

