## Database Schema Versioning & Migrations

Mobile binary updates must never crash or wipe local user data due to unhandled database schema changes:

<DiagramExpand title="DATABASE SCHEMA MIGRATION LIFECYCLE">

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    V1["Schema Version 1\n(Shipped in App v1.0)"] -->|"Migration 1 to 2\n(Add nullable column)"| V2
    V2["Schema Version 2\n(Shipped in App v1.1)"] -->|"Migration 2 to 3\n(Add table & index)"| V3
    V3["Schema Version 3\n(Shipped in App v2.0)"]

    classDef v1 fill:#ede9fe,stroke:#8b5cf6,stroke-width:2px,color:#4c1d95;
    classDef v2 fill:#e0f2fe,stroke:#0284c7,stroke-width:2px,color:#0369a1;
    classDef v3 fill:#dcfce7,stroke:#16a34a,stroke-width:2px,color:#14532d;

    class V1 v1;
    class V2 v2;
    class V3 v3;
```

</DiagramExpand>

### Mandatory Migration Rules
1. **Zero Destructive Fallbacks in Production:** Android's `.fallbackToDestructiveMigration()` or unversioned store replacement is strictly prohibited in release builds.
2. **Nullable Columns for Schema Expansion:** All newly introduced columns must be `NULLABLE` or specify a safe default value.
3. **Automated Migration Test Suites:** Every schema modification PR must include an automated migration unit test verifying that existing records upgrade cleanly from version $N-1$ to $N$.

---

## Architectural Non-Negotiables

<Aside type="danger" title="PERSISTENCE VIOLATIONS">
The following anti-patterns trigger automatic PR review rejection:

1. **Main Thread Database I/O:** Never execute SQLite queries, CoreData fetches, or disk writes on the UI main thread. All database calls must execute on background threads (`Dispatchers.IO` in Kotlin, background Swift actors, asynchronous JavaScript threads).
2. **Plain-Text Credentials in Database:** User tokens, passwords, and private API keys must never be stored in plain database columns or unencrypted storage. Tokens belong exclusively in Android KeyStore or iOS Keychain.
3. **Missing Idempotency Keys:** Every mutating outbox record must generate a unique client UUID sent via the `X-Idempotency-Key` header to prevent duplicate server actions during network reconnects.
4. **Unconstrained Caching:** All cached entity stores must specify time-to-live (TTL) limits or eviction rules to prevent application binary bloat and operating system storage purges.
</Aside>

---

## Quality Gate PR Merge Checklist

Before submitting code introducing or modifying offline storage logic, verify every requirement:

- [ ] **Offline Launch Tested:** Application launches, renders cached records, and accepts offline inputs with device radio disabled.
- [ ] **Idempotency Header Included:** Outbox synchronization transmits a unique client UUID in `X-Idempotency-Key`.
- [ ] **Background Thread Dispatching:** All SQLite, Room, or CoreData operations execute off the main UI thread.
- [ ] **Migration Test Added:** Database schema increments include an automated unit test verifying data retention from prior versions.
- [ ] **Encrypted Storage for Secrets:** Sensitive tokens reside strictly in hardware-backed storage (Keychain / KeyStore).




